				<p class="text-sm text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Rail transit fares in the Greater Manila Area are statutory public tariffs regulated by the <strong>Department of Transportation (DOTr)</strong> and the <strong>Light Rail Transit Authority (LRTA)</strong>. Fares are constructed using a two-part tariff consisting of a <em>boarding fee</em> (flagdown rate) plus a distance-based <em>per-kilometer rate</em>.
