				</div>
				<p class="text-xs text-mapa-clay leading-relaxed">
					<em>Note:</em> Single Journey Tickets (paper magnetics / QR tokens) are rounded up to the nearest 5-peso denomination under LRTA guidelines to simplify cash handling at passenger ticket sales offices (TSO). Using an electronic stored-value beep™ card guarantees the exact statutory centavo computation and avoids token queues.
				</p>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 2: Statutory 20% Discounts -->
			<section>
				<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
					2. Statutory 20% Discount Rights (Students, Seniors, PWDs)
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					By national law, all public rail transit operators in the Philippines must provide a 20% discount on standard commuter tariffs:
				</p>
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
					<div class="bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour/70 rounded-xl p-4">
						<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Students (RA 11314)</h3>
						<p class="text-mapa-ink/75 leading-relaxed">
							Applies to all Filipino students from primary to undergraduate tertiary and technical-vocational levels. Valid <strong>365 days a year</strong> including weekends, semestral breaks, and national holidays.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour/70 rounded-xl p-4">
						<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Senior Citizens (RA 9994)</h3>
						<p class="text-mapa-ink/75 leading-relaxed">
							All Filipino citizens aged 60 years and above are entitled to 20% off all rail fares and exemption from value-added tax upon showing an OSCA ID or valid Philippine passport.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="bg-mapa-canvas border border-mapa-contour/70 rounded-xl p-4">
						<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Persons with Disabilities (RA 10754)</h3>
						<p class="text-mapa-ink/75 leading-relaxed">
							Eligible PWDs presenting a valid PDAO (Persons with Disability Affairs Office) ID or National Council on Disability Affairs (NCDA) card receive 20% discount and priority car access.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 3: beep Card Commuter Guide -->
			<section>
				<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
					3. beep™ Card Rules, Expiration, and Reloading
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					The contactless contactless smart card system (operated by AF Payments Inc.) is interoperable across LRT-1, LRT-2, MRT-3, EDSA Carousel buses, BGC Bus, and select modern PUVs:
				</p>
				<ul class="space-y-3 text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 list-disc pl-5 leading-relaxed">
					<li>
						<strong>Card Validity:</strong> Standard blue beep cards are valid for <strong>4 years</strong> from issuance. You can extend an expiring card for an additional 1 year at any station Teller Ticket Booth for a nominal ₱10 extension fee.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Concessionary Cards:</strong> White/Gold Concessionary beep cards are personalized for Seniors and PWDs, encoding the 20% discount automatically at turnstiles without needing ticket window verification on each trip.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Minimum Balance Requirement:</strong> To enter turnstiles, a card must have at least the minimum boarding fee of the line (₱15 on LRT-1, ₱13 on MRT-3, ₱14 on LRT-2). If your exit station incurs a higher fare than your balance, the turnstile will reject exit until you reload at the station excess fare booth.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 4: Baggage, Bicycles & Commuter Etiquette -->
			<section>
				<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
